   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Possessives: mein, dein…",
     "texto": [
      "Possessives take endings similar to **ein**. The ending depends on the gender and number of the noun and on the case: **mein Sofa**, **meine Lampe**, **meine Freunde**. The possessor determines the stem (**mein-**, **dein-**, **unser-**, **Ihr-**); the object determines the ending."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Possessives in the most common cases",
     "texto": [
      "In the nominative: **mein Vater**, **meine Mutter**, **mein Kind**, **meine Freunde**. In the accusative the masculine changes: **Ich suche meinen Schlüssel**; in the dative: **mit meinem Freund**, **mit meiner Schwester**, **mit meinem Kind**, **mit meinen Freunden**. In the dative plural the noun usually adds **-n**: **Freunden**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
